  "worked_solution": "The order of a recurrence relation is the largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding terms in the relation.\n\nLet's examine each recurrence relation in turn.\n\n- The largest index difference between ${a}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${a}_{n-1}$ in the relation is $1.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $1.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${b}_{n}$ and the preceding terms ${b}_{n-1}$ and ${b}_{n-3}$ in the relation is $3.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $3.$\n\n- The largest index difference between ${c}_{n}$ and the preceding term ${c}_{n-1}$ in the relation is $1.$ So, this recurrence relation has order $1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
